      "tested_by_leonardo": "No direct test record established in the inspected sources.",
      "built_in_lifetime": "[museum] The San Marco lock was real. Bartolomeo Della Valle built the linking locks. The catalogue explicitly allows either an improvement or a survey by Leonardo. [gates] Preserved gate timber spans the sixteenth to nineteenth centuries.",
      "later_tests": [
        "[gates] Museum material investigations in 2016 examined the historic gate components. This is conservation evidence, not a controlled test of a Leonardo prototype."
      ]
